---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SmoothInteractions from "../../components/wellington/SmoothInteractions.astro";
import FAQ from "../../components/wellington/FAQ.astro";
import "../../styles/wellington.css";
import "../../styles/wellington-editorial.css";
import "../../styles/wellington-illustration.css";
const benefits=[
 {title:"Hand over more.",copy:"The aim is to let Wellington handle useful work within the boundaries you set, without asking you to approve every small step.",path:"M5 12h14m-5-5 5 5-5 5"},
 {title:"Catch the wrong turn.",copy:"Check what an action could affect before it changes something you care about.",path:"m12 3 9 4v5c0 5-9 9-9 9s-9-4-9-9V7l9-4Zm-4 9 3 3 5-6"},
 {title:"Keep your say.",copy:"Bring you in when the facts or permissions leave a real decision to make, with a clear reason why.",path:"M4 5h16v11H9l-5 4V5Zm4 4h8m-8 3h5"}
];
const examples=[
 {title:"Make room for life.",request:"“Give me some breathing room next week.”",check:"A free afternoon is not permission to cancel a commitment.",result:"Move flexible work. Keep the promises."},
 {title:"Keep important things intact.",request:"“Tidy up this project.”",check:"A file that looks old may still be needed by another person or system.",result:"Check what depends on it before changing it."},
 {title:"Share with care.",request:"“Get the team up to speed.”",check:"Information you can access is not always information you can share.",result:"Check the people and material involved."}
];
const questions=[
 {question:"Is Sapiens working inside Wellington today?",answer:"The integration is in development. Wellington is in internal testing ahead of a private alpha. Sending messages and changing calendar events still require confirmation. The illustrations on this page show intended behavior using fictional scenarios."},
 {question:"How much would Sapiens need to know?",answer:"We’re starting with a defined set of resources Wellington can use, the instructions and permissions that apply, and the relevant connections between them. The approach depends on the information available. It does not assume a complete picture of your life."},
 {question:"What happens when information is missing?",answer:"The intended behavior is to pause and ask for the specific fact or approval needed. Missing information should not silently become permission to proceed."},
 {question:"Does this replace privacy and security controls?",answer:"No. Action checks still need secure account connections, access controls and reliable enforcement. They cannot guarantee that every possible consequence is known."}
];
---
<Base title="Wellington Governance" description="Meet Sapiens, the system we’re developing to help Wellington take on useful work within the boundaries you set." cta={false} socialImage="/wellington/app-icon.png" socialImageAlt="Wellington logo" socialCard="summary">
<div class="we-page atlas-page">
 <header class="atlas-hero wrap">
  <h1>Off your plate.<br/><span>On your terms.</span></h1>
  <p>More help shouldn’t mean more supervision. Meet Sapiens, the system we’re developing to help Wellington take care of more while respecting the boundaries you set.</p>
  <a class="atlas-button" href="#atlas-approach">Explore the approach <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M10 4v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5"/></svg></a>
 </header>
 <div class="wrap">
  <figure class="atlas-visual" aria-label="Concept illustration: Sapiens checks a proposed project cleanup against instructions before allowing a revised action.">
   <div class="atlas-contours" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
   <div class="atlas-context atlas-context-one"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 3h9l5 5v13H5V3Zm9 0v6h5M8 13h8m-8 4h5"/></svg><span>Project files<strong>Shared originals</strong></span></div>
   <div class="atlas-context atlas-context-two"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m12 3 9 4v5c0 5-9 9-9 9s-9-4-9-9V7l9-4Zm-4 9 3 3 5-6"/></svg><span>Your instruction<strong>Ask before deleting</strong></span></div>
   <div class="atlas-center">
    <div class="atlas-request">“Organize this project for me.”</div>
    <div class="atlas-check"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 50 50"><circle cx="25" cy="25" r="19"/><path d="m16 25 6 6 13-14"/></svg><div><strong>Sapiens</strong><span>Does the next step fit?</span></div></div>
    <div class="atlas-result"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Archive the copies. Keep the originals.</strong><span>The proposed cleanup respects your instruction.</span></div></div>
   </div>
   <figcaption>Illustrative concept. Sapiens integration is in development.</figcaption>
  </figure>
 </div>
 <section class="atlas-section wrap" aria-labelledby="benefit-heading">
  <div class="atlas-intro"><h2 id="benefit-heading">More room for you.<br/><span>Less to watch over.</span></h2><p>We want assistants to take work off your hands without making you keep watch over everything they do. Sapiens is how we’re exploring that next step.</p></div>
  <div class="atlas-benefits">{benefits.map(item=><article><svg class="atlas-icon" viewBox="0 0 26 26" aria-hidden="true"><path d={item.path}/></svg><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.copy}</p></article>)}</div>
 </section>
 <section class="atlas-section atlas-approach" id="atlas-approach" aria-labelledby="approach-heading"><div class="wrap">
  <h2 id="approach-heading">Your intentions.<br/><span>Carried into the next step.</span></h2>
  <div class="atlas-split">
   <div class="atlas-map" role="img" aria-label="Your instructions, relevant facts and granted permissions inform a check of the next action, leading to proceed, revise or ask.">
    <div class="atlas-map-inputs"><span>Your instructions</span><span>The relevant facts</span><span>Your permissions</span></div><div class="atlas-map-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="atlas-map-core"><span>Sapiens</span><strong>Check the next action</strong></div><div class="atlas-map-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="atlas-map-outputs"><span>Proceed</span><span>Revise</span><span>Ask you</span></div>
   </div>
   <div class="atlas-feature-list">
    <details open name="atlas-features"><summary><h3>Check what you meant.</h3><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Compare the proposed action with your request. “Find a few options” should not quietly become a purchase. “Prepare this” should not become “publish it.”</p></details>
    <details name="atlas-features"><summary><h3>See what it could affect.</h3><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Look at the relevant files, accounts, people and commitments. A change that seems small in one place can matter somewhere else.</p></details>
    <details name="atlas-features"><summary><h3>Know when to bring you in.</h3><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>If the action goes beyond the authority you gave, or a necessary fact is missing, ask a focused question. Explain what needs your decision.</p></details>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div></section>
 <section class="atlas-section wrap" aria-labelledby="everyday-heading">
  <div class="atlas-intro"><h2 id="everyday-heading">Built for the things<br/><span>you hand over.</span></h2><p>Different tasks. The same principle: useful help should respect what matters to you. These scenarios show the behavior we’re working toward.</p></div>
  <div class="atlas-examples">{examples.map((item,index)=><article>
   <div class="atlas-example-art" aria-hidden="true">
    {index===0 && <div class="atlas-week"><span>Keep</span><strong>Family time</strong><span>Move</span><strong>Flexible work <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M3 10h14m-5-5 5 5-5 5"/></svg></strong></div>}
    {index===1 && <div class="atlas-files"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 32 38"><path d="M3 1h17l9 9v27H3V1Zm17 0v10h9M9 19h14M9 25h10"/></svg><span>Original</span></div><div><svg viewBox="0 0 32 38"><path d="M3 1h17l9 9v27H3V1Zm17 0v10h9M9 19h14M9 25h10"/></svg><span>Copy</span></div></div>}
    {index===2 && <div class="atlas-sharing"><span>Private notes</span><div></div><strong>Team update <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m4 10 4 4 8-8"/></svg></strong></div>}
   </div><h3>{item.title}</h3><blockquote>{item.request}</blockquote><p>{item.check}</p><p class="atlas-example-result">{item.result}</p>
  </article>)}</div>
 </section>
 <section class="atlas-underhood" aria-labelledby="underhood-heading"><div class="wrap atlas-split">
  <div><h2 id="underhood-heading">What’s behind<br/><span>the decision?</span></h2><p>Sapiens checks a proposed action before a tool carries it out. We’re developing the approach in a defined Wellington workspace, starting with the resources it can actually use.</p><a class="atlas-link" href="/wellington/">Meet Wellington <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M4 10h12m-5-5 5 5-5 5"/></svg></a></div>
  <div class="atlas-technical-list"><article><h3>A connected picture.</h3><p>Represent the relevant resources and their relationships, along with the instructions and permissions that apply.</p></article><article><h3>A reasoned check.</h3><p>We’re exploring New Sapience’s Sapiens technology to assess proposed actions against those facts. Technical access and licensing remain to be established.</p></article><article><h3>A decision that takes effect.</h3><p>The tool must enforce the result before execution. Checking an explanation alone is not enough; the actual action has to match.</p></article></div>
 </div></section>
 <section class="atlas-section wrap" aria-labelledby="development-heading"><div class="atlas-intro"><h2 id="development-heading">Start with useful work.<br/><span>Show what improves.</span></h2><p>The next proposed milestone is one complete Wellington workflow in a controlled workspace. We’ll test the decisions and compare the effort with existing permission and approval checks.</p></div><div class="atlas-measures"><article><h3>Does the work get done?</h3><p>Let legitimate actions proceed without adding unnecessary questions or delay.</p></article><article><h3>Do the checks help?</h3><p>Catch consequential mistakes and explain why an action needs to change.</p></article><article><h3>Is there less to manage?</h3><p>Measure the effort people spend reviewing, correcting and supervising the work.</p></article></div></section>
 <FAQ id="governance-faq" questions={questions}/>
 <section class="atlas-close"><div class="wrap"><h2>Help shape<br/><span>what happens next.</span></h2><p>Follow Wellington’s progress as we build toward more useful help, on your terms.</p><a class="atlas-button" href="/wellington/#wellington-signup-form">Get alpha updates <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M4 10h12m-5-5 5 5-5 5"/></svg></a></div></section>
</div>
 <SmoothInteractions/>
</Base>
<style>
